_refine.details                                  
;1. HYDROGENS HAVE BEEN ADDED IN THE RIDING POSITIONS. 2. RESIDUES 1-15 IN CHAIN A, 1-17 IN CHAIN B AND C, AND 1-17 AND 227-229 IN CHAIN D ARE DISORDERED AND NOT INCLUDED IN THE MODEL. 3. A MG ION FROM THE CRYSTALLIZATION SOLUTION IS OCTAHEDERALLY COORDINATED TO THE SIDECHAINS OF ASP 25 AND ASP 200, THE BACKBONE CARBONYL OXYGEN OF GLU 27, AND THREE WATER MOLECULES. 4. A PEG 3350 MOLECULE FROM THE CRYSTALLIZATION SOLUTION IS LOCATED NEAR VAL 114 IN SUBUNIT A, AND IS PARTIALLY MODELED AS PE4. 5. UNEXPLAINED DIFFERENCE DENSITY IN THE VICINITY OF THE SIDECHAINS OF HIS 79 AND GLU 82 ON THE D SUBUNIT WAS OBSERVED, AND THIS DENSITY WAS NOT MODELED.
;
